timer-project/
│
├── README.md             # Project overview, usage, setup instructions
├── LICENSE               # License file (MIT, GPL, etc.)
├── .gitignore            # Ignore build files, temp files, etc.
│
├── src/                  # Main source code
│   ├── main.py           # Entry point (Python) OR main.ino (Arduino)
│   ├── timer.py          # Timer logic (start, stop, reset, countdown)
│   ├── ui.py             # Optional - GUI or console interface
│   └── utils.py          # Helper functions
│
├── assets/               # Icons, sounds, images (if GUI/web)
│   └── alarm.wav
│
├── tests/                # Unit tests
│   ├── test_timer.py
│   └── ...
│
├── hardware/             # (if microcontroller project)
│   ├── schematics.png    # Circuit diagram
│   ├── wiring.txt        # Pin connections
│   └── notes.md          # Hardware-related documentation
│
└── docs/                 # Documentation
    ├── design.md         # Project design details
    └── usage.md          # How to use the timer
🔑 Explanation of Files
README.md → Description, setup, and usage instructions (first thing people see).

src/ → Core code (Python, C, C++, JS, or Arduino).

tests/ → Unit tests to check timer accuracy & logic.

assets/ → Extra resources like icons, sounds (for alarms).

hardware/ → Only if it’s an embedded project (Arduino, ESP32, STM32).

docs/ → Detailed documentation (optional, but good for GitHub).

LICENSE → Always include a license so others know how they can use your code.
